# Explorer stage (Energy is the standard)

Read `docs/visual-identity.md` › Explorer. **Energy & Industry** is the locked behaviour to copy — especially Consumption (`ConsumptionCanvas.tsx`, `ConsumptionAppetite.tsx`) and Generation (`GenerationCanvas.tsx`). Housing domains that still put controls or method essays inside the Stage body are **drift**; bring them into line with Energy, do not copy the drift.

## Frame order (locked)

`ExplorerHead` (view tabs) → `FigureStrip` → `ControlRow` of `MenuControl`s (+ `ResetButton`) → `<Stage title meta foot={…}>` → body.

- Filters and period/place menus live in the **outer** `ControlRow`, never inside the Stage body.
- Patent detail lives in **one** stage foot only (below).

## One Notes foot — never two

- Patent detail (definition, method, derived totals, caveats, provisional meaning) lives in **one** stage foot: `FigureRecord` **or** `SourceLine` (which builds a `FigureRecord`).
- Put that foot on `<Stage foot={…}>`. Do **not** also render `SourceLine` / `FigureRecord` below the stage.
- Do **not** paste definition/method essays into the plot body or callout boxes inside the stage.
- Do **not** render the explorer `<Coverage>` facts strip (`SPAN` / `OBSERVATIONS` / …) on sector domain stages. Energy does not. Span, unit and geography sit in the stage bar meta and Notes when needed.
- **Source line** (every sector): `Publisher · series · [Boundaries: …] · geography · [period]` via `formatSource`. Never smash publisher into the series name. Full citations only on Data provenance desks.

## Multi-chart titles (Consumption / Housing pipeline pattern)

- Separate charts with `<section>` + `<h3 className={explorerClasses.stageTitle}>…</h3>` (sentence case).
- Do **not** use `.bo-label` “FIG. 1 · …” caps for chart titles — that is index/label type, not section titles.
- Reference: Energy Consumption Metabolism panels; Housing supply `view === "pipeline"` only as a secondary multi-chart example.

## Briefs do not override the shell

- A Notion brief ("signature design", "woven ribbons", "split flow") changes **content**, not the frame. Build the tab as Consumption Metabolism / Appetite do: outer `ControlRow`, then Stage body as `s.stack` of `s.panel` sections, `stageTitle`, shared `TimeChart` / `RankBars` / `ChangeRows`.
- At most one custom instrument per tab, one ink (stipple / sparse dots / hatch / cross / engrave). Never chart colours, gutter end labels, axis markers, value legends or "exact values" drawers in a custom view.
- Claude Code: use the `exchange-domain-view` skill (`.claude/skills/exchange-domain-view/SKILL.md`) for any domain-tab change.

## Width

- Every panel and instrument figure is `width: 100%; min-width: 0` inside the stage body.
- RankBars and TimeChart have different **internal** gutters by design (name column vs axis margin). Outer frames share the stage edge; do not invent a second chart frame or inset.
- Multi-series **line** charts use `SeriesLegend` under the plot for names and latest values so the **plot fills the stage**. Do not put series names in-plot on stacks.
- End-of-line leaders: default **off**. The plot fills the stage; `SeriesLegend` under the plot carries names and latest values. Pass `leaders={true}` only when end labels are deliberate. MixLines keeps fuel names in its own legend above the chart — no 150px gutter.
- **Do not patch empty right strips view-by-view.** If a `TimeChart` looks short of the stage edge, it is almost always still drawing end leaders or a reserved gutter — set `leaders` false (the default) or fix `chartMargins`, do not add local CSS width hacks.

## Data tab — observation tables, not catalogue dumps

- A Data view shows **observation / series tables** when Ready series exist. Reference: Energy Consumption / Generation Data, Housing Land (`land/LandData.tsx`), Housing Prices Data.
- Body uses `explorerClasses.tableGroup` + `stageTitle` + `tableWrap` / `table` (optional series `MenuControl` in the **outer** ControlRow). One table per dataset or frequency.
- **Forbidden as a Data body:** “Ready catalogue records” link lists. Catalogue links belong in the Notes foot / row links / Data →, not as the whole stage.
- No observations yet → `<EmptyStage>` (“In preparation”), never a catalogue dump or a `data/...json` path on screen.

## Exact values / Exact register — closed disclosures

- Chart exact values stay inside TimeChart’s built-in disclosure.
- Event / policy **exact registers** use brand `ExactRegister` (`web/src/brand/policy/`): closed by default, `.bo-disclosure` summary, table inside. Never an always-on competing layout under the ledger.

## Policy / event domains — Decision Ledger

- Must use brand `DecisionLedger` + `CatalogueDossier` from `web/src/brand/policy/` (electric closed slab → paper open → Interior 3 catalogue card).
- Do **not** fork slab CSS, invent a parallel dossier, or restyle the register. Map sector event records into the shared view-model; keep connectors/data in the sector tree.
- References for new work: **charts** = Consumption / Generation; **Data** = Consumption Data / Land / Generation; **policy** = brand Decision Ledger.
